      "text": "To solve for the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\), we need to analyze the given information and the properties of angles in a straight line.\n\n1. **Identify the given information:**\n   - \\(RSP\\) is a straight line.\n   - \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Understand the properties of angles in a straight line:**\n   - Co-interior angles (also known as same-side interior angles) formed by two parallel lines cut by a transversal are supplementary. This means their measures add up to \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\n3. **Determine the relationship between \\(\\angle QSP\\) and the adjacent angle \\(\\angle PQR\\):**\n   - \\(\\angle QSP\\) and \\(\\angle PQR\\) are co-interior angles because \\(RSP\\) is a straight line.\n   - Therefore, \\(\\angle QSP\\) and \\(\\angle PQR\\) are supplementary:\n     \\[\n     \\angle QSP + \\angle PQR = 180^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n4. **Substitute the given value of \\(\\angle QSP\\):**\n   \\[\n   80^\\circ + \\angle PQR = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n5. **Solve for \\(\\angle PQR\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQR = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{100}\\) degrees.",
