      "text": "To find the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\), we will use the properties of angles and straight lines in the given diagram. Here is the step-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. **Identify the given information:**\n   - \\(RSP\\) is a straight line.\n   - \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Determine the measure of \\(\\angle QRS\\):**\n   Since \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, the sum of the angles on a straight line is \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore, we can write:\n   \\[\n   \\angle QSP + \\angle QRS = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   Given \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\), we substitute this value into the equation:\n   \\[\n   80^\\circ + \\angle QRS = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\(\\angle QRS\\):\n   \\[\n   \\angle QRS = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\):**\n   We need to find the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\). To do this, we will use the fact that \\(\\angle PQR\\) and \\(\\angle QRS\\) are supplementary angles (they add up to \\(180^\\circ\\)):\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQR + \\angle QRS = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   Substituting the value of \\(\\angle QRS\\) from the previous step:\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQR + 100^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\(\\angle PQR\\):\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQR = 180^\\circ - 100^\\circ = 80^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{80}\\).",
