      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\). Let's break down the steps and reasoning:\n\n1. **Identify the given information and the diagram:**\n   - \\(RSP\\) is a straight line.\n   - \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Understand the properties of angles in a straight line:**\n   - A straight line forms a \\(180^\\circ\\) angle.\n   - The sum of the angles on a straight line is \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\n3. **Find \\(\\angle PSQ\\):**\n   - Since \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, \\(\\angle PSQ\\) is the supplementary angle to \\(\\angle QSP\\).\n   \\[\n   \\angle PSQ = 180^\\circ - \\angle QSP\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\angle PSQ = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine \\(\\angle PQS\\):**\n   - \\(\\angle PQS\\) is an exterior angle to \\(\\triangle PQS\\) at point \\(P\\).\n   - The measure of an exterior angle of a triangle is equal to the sum of the measures of the two non-adjacent interior angles.\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQS = \\angle PSQ + \\angle QPS\n   \\]\n   - Given \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle PSQ = 100^\\circ\\), we need to find \\(\\angle QPS\\).\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQS = 100^\\circ + \\angle QPS\n   \\]\n\n5. **Express \\(\\angle PQR\\) in terms of \\(\\angle QPS\\):**\n   - \\(\\angle PQR\\) is the same as \\(\\angle PQS\\) because they are vertically opposite angles formed by the intersection of the lines.\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQR = \\angle PQS\n   \\]\n   - From the previous step, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQS = 100^\\circ + \\angle QPS\n   \\]\n   - Since \\(\\angle QPS\\) is part of the straight line and not directly given, we use the fact that \\(\\angle PSQ\\) and \\(\\angle PQS\\) are supplementary.\n\n6. **Final calculation:**\n   - From the supplementary angles:\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQR = \\angle PQS = 100^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{80}\\).",
